<title>FRANCE: Europcar, BA French units in partnership.</title>
<headline>Europcar, BA French units in partnership.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-03-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Europcar, a car rental company owned jointly by Accor and Volkswagen, said on Tuesday it had struck an exclusive partnership deal with British Airways' French subsidiaries TAT and Air Liberte.</p>
<p>&quot;TAT and Air Liberte invited offers for an exclusive partnership with a car rental firm. We've just won against Avis,&quot; a Europcar spokeswoman told Reuters.</p>
<p>Under the deal, Europcar rentals would be proposed to TAT and Air Liberte passengers, who would receive discount rates. An official at Accor said the deal could be expanded to include its hotels and travel agencies.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom, +33 1 4221 5452</p>
